  "Question": "A rectangular photograph is placed in a frame that forms a border two inches wide on all sides of the photograph. The photograph measures \\(8\\) inches high and \\(10\\) inches wide. What is the area of the border, in square inches?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( 36 \\)",
    "B": "\\( 40 \\)",
    "C": "\\( 64 \\)",
    "D": "\\( 72 \\)",
    "E": "\\( 88 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The border adds \\(2\\) inches at both ends of each dimension. Thus the outside rectangle is \\(8+2+2=12\\) inches high and \\(10+2+2=14\\) inches wide.\n\nSubtracting the photograph’s area from the outside rectangle’s area leaves exactly the border:\n\\[\n12\\cdot14-8\\cdot10=168-80=88.\n\\]\nThe border has area \\(88\\) square inches, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
